## 🔐 OS & Cybersecurity

Understanding Operating Systems is essential for cybersecurity because security professionals need to understand:

- How processes run
- How memory is managed
- How files are stored and accessed
- How users and permissions work
- How applications interact with the OS
- How the OS communicates with hardware
- Where security vulnerabilities can occur
- How access control helps protect systems

> Strong Operating System fundamentals → Stronger cybersecurity foundation.

